> Questions:
> 1. Other than the 2 you start with, how does one make Potions of
> Vampire Blood?

Drain your own blood (once you have a medecine bag) with the appropriate  
technique.
You'll also lose a level, but that can be good in the early game.
Don't forget to bless vampire blood so they'll also act as gain level...
And you'll find blood/vampire blood on Vampires (eg, in the chaotic  
quest...)

> 2. I've noticed sometimes when attacking I become satiated
> momentarily.  I'm guessing my 'bite' attack when successful provides
> some sustenance.  How much?  Is it only the first bite per creature or
> multiple bites?  What would happen if I am 100% satiated - is there a
> danger of choking?  Does a "oMB prevent this?

You gain nutrition by bitting but won't bite yourself to indigestion.
And won't bite cockatrice either, for that matter.
(this only apply if your base race is vampire, not is polymorphed into  
one).

> 3. I am unable to drink from a fountain as it says I am flying (which
> I am), but I can eat corpses off the ground and pick items up - why
> cant I drink from a fountain?  I'm also not able to retreive items in
> the bottom of a pit, but I CAN fly down a trapdoor using ">".

